WEBVTT

NOTE English translation of the Vietnamese narration script. Timing is distributed proportionally within each slide segment, since the narration itself is in Vietnamese.

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.684
Hello everyone, this is the guide video for Lab 2:

2
00:00:03.684 --> 00:00:05.578
Drafting administrative documents.

3
00:00:05.578 --> 00:00:10.200
In this lab you'll draft five types of documents used every day in any organisation.

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.981
Let's start with a decision.

5
00:00:13.981 --> 00:00:16.537
The “Căn cứ” (basis) section follows a set pattern:

6
00:00:16.537 --> 00:00:20.696
“Pursuant to the document defining functions and duties;” “Pursuant to the relevant

7
00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:24.755
specialised regulation;” “Considering the proposal from...” Each line ends with a

8
00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:25.257
semicolon,

9
00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:26.760
the last one with a full stop.

10
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.496
Then comes the word “QUYẾT ĐỊ NH” (DECIDES), capitalised, bold and centred,

11
00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:31.990
followed by numbered Articles.

12
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:36.578
The final Article always states the effective date and who is responsible for implementation.

13
00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:40.459
A common mistake is using the word “request” inside a decision — that's wrong;

14
00:00:40.459 --> 00:00:42.400
a decision must use directive language.

15
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.578
A proposal memo has three parts.

16
00:00:46.578 --> 00:00:49.633
The opening states the basis and the current situation.

17
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:53.554
The body presents a specific plan: quantity, estimated cost, timeline,

18
00:00:53.554 --> 00:00:56.411
along with an analysis of benefits and feasibility.

19
00:00:56.411 --> 00:01:01.522
It closes with a line respectfully requesting the competent authority to review and approve.

20
00:01:01.522 --> 00:01:06.300
Don't forget to attach a cost estimate — this is the mistake students make most often.

21
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.475
An official letter has a distinctive feature: it has no type heading.

22
00:01:12.475 --> 00:01:16.990
That means there's no large word “CÔNG VĂN” (OFFICIAL LETTER) in the middle — only

23
00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:21.339
a reference number and a summary line starting with “V/v”, meaning “regarding”.

24
00:01:21.339 --> 00:01:24.054
A request letter opens with the basis and reason,

25
00:01:24.054 --> 00:01:26.990
states the request along with a deadline in the body,

26
00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:30.093
and closes with “Trân trọng./.”, meaning “Respectfully”.

27
00:01:30.093 --> 00:01:33.321
A reply letter opens with: “In reply to Official Letter No.

28
00:01:33.321 --> 00:01:35.564
..., dated ..., from ..., regarding ...”.

29
00:01:35.564 --> 00:01:38.300
Remember: each letter should cover only one topic.

30
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.820
Minutes and reports.

31
00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.544
Minutes open with the time, place and attendees;

32
00:01:44.544 --> 00:01:48.630
the body records each person's remarks in order, briefly and faithfully;

33
00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:53.284
it closes with the chair's conclusion, a line stating what time the meeting ended,

34
00:01:53.284 --> 00:01:56.405
that the minutes were read back to everyone and agreed,

35
00:01:56.405 --> 00:01:59.299
then the signatures of the secretary and the chair.

36
00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:03.165
Whoever takes the minutes must never add their own personal comments.

37
00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:07.170
A report follows a four-part flow: the situation, the results achieved,

38
00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:11.400
the limitations and their causes, and the way forward with recommendations.

39
00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.026
Assignment 2: based on the situation where the Accounting Department of An Phat Co.

40
00:02:18.026 --> 00:02:19.315
needs ten more computers,

41
00:02:19.315 --> 00:02:23.389
each of you will draw two of the five document types — proposal memo, decision,

42
00:02:23.389 --> 00:02:25.968
official letter, minutes, report — and draft them.

43
00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:30.805
They must follow the correct format under Decree 30 and the distinctive structure of each type.

44
00:02:30.805 --> 00:02:33.119
Submit a Word file by the end of the session,

45
00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.794
then revise it based on my feedback within one week.
